    "notes": "Payroll statutory structure and values for companies in the DR Congo (docs/modules/payroll.md, PAY-07, PAY-08, PAY-21). Each period has a status (ResearchStatus): 'researched' values come from public research (docs/country-packs-research-2026-10.md) with their confidence (high or medium), research date and sources; they are used, and every run that uses one records it and shows the 'from public research' notice until the owner confirms the value through a pack release (ADM-04). 'assumed' lists a researched period's fields that are conservative defaults pending confirmation (CNSS not deducted from the IPR base; rounding to the franc, the currency's unit, where no rule was found). A value that is null is 'rate needed' and blocks payroll runs; low-confidence research is never entered (it may be noted with confidence 'low' and its sources). A component with 'unconfirmed: not_applied' is left out of runs while unconfirmed instead of blocking them (IPR dependants: no reduction until confirmed). A component with 'may_not_apply' may be marked 'not applicable' by a company in its payroll settings (audited); otherwise it blocks runs until confirmed (INPP). Every money figure is per month in minor units of the pack currency (CDF, no decimals) as a digit string; the IPR bands are the annual bands divided by 12 (exact). Rates are percentages as strings ('12.5' = 12.5 %). Salaries paid in another currency (e.g. USD) are converted to CDF at the company's rate on the pay date before these figures apply. effective_from 2026-01-01 is the date this pack's data starts, not the date any law took effect. rounding is {mode: half_up|down|up, unit_minor: digits} applied once to the component's result. Labels live in lang/{locale}/payroll.php (pack.*).",
